type: software

title: "SE Theory: Transformation"
version: "0.6.1" # CUSTOM: Updated to match the current release version of the project
date-released: "2026-10-30" # CUSTOM: Updated to match the current release date of the project

authors:
  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, School of Computer Science and Information Systems, Maryville, MO, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-theory-transformation"
url: "https://github.com/structural-explainability/se-theory-transformation"

license: Apache-2.0

abstract: >
  Lean 4 formalization of foundational transformation theory for
  Structural Explainability. This repository defines transformation
  operators, families, kinds, operator-family-kind mappings,
  atomic effect semantics, effect dimensions, operator footprints,
  required-change conditions, finite sequences of atomic steps,
  composition and orthogonality relations, finite invariants,
  reference declarations, and machine-readable transformation registries.

keywords:
  - structural-explainability
  - transformation-theory
  - transformation-operators
  - transformation-families
  - transformation-kinds
  - effect-semantics
  - effect-dimensions
  - operator-footprints
  - required-change-conditions
  - atomic-steps
  - sequence-footprint-upper-bounds
  - composition
  - orthogonality
  - operator-registry
  - machine-readable-semantics
  - lean4
  - theorem-proving
  - formal-verification
  - proof-carrying
